// @expect-error Variable 'named' has type 'Named', but its value has type 'T'. 'T' can be any type that implements 'Named', including a struct. A value of type 'Named' must be an object of a class, and a struct value is not one. Declare 'named' as a 'T', or bound 'T' by a class that implements 'Named', as in '<T: Person>'.
// @expect-error 'named' has type 'Named', but the value assigned to it has type 'T'. 'T' can be any type that implements 'Named', including a struct. A value of type 'Named' must be an object of a class, and a struct value is not one. Declare 'named' as a 'T', or bound 'T' by a class that implements 'Named', as in '<T: Person>'.
// @expect-error 'holder.named' has type 'Named?', but the value assigned to it has type 'T'. 'T' can be any type that implements 'Named', including a struct. A value of type 'Named' must be an object of a class, and a struct value is not one. Bound 'T' by a class that implements 'Named', as in '<T: Person>'.
// @expect-error Argument 1 of 'greet' has type 'T', but parameter 'named' has type 'Named'. 'T' can be any type that implements 'Named', including a struct. A value of type 'Named' must be an object of a class, and a struct value is not one. Declare '<T: Named>' after 'greet' and declare parameter 'named' as 'T', or bound 'T' by a class that implements 'Named', as in '<T: Person>'.
// @expect-error Argument 1 of 'set' has type 'T', but parameter 'named' has type 'Named'. 'T' can be any type that implements 'Named', including a struct. A value of type 'Named' must be an object of a class, and a struct value is not one. Bound 'T' by a class that implements 'Named', as in '<T: Person>'.
// @expect-error Argument 1 of the constructor of 'Holder' has type 'T', but parameter 'named' has type 'Named'. 'T' can be any type that implements 'Named', including a struct. A value of type 'Named' must be an object of a class, and a struct value is not one. Bound 'T' by a class that implements 'Named', as in '<T: Person>'.
// @expect-error Function 'returned' returns 'Named', but this value has type 'T'. 'T' can be any type that implements 'Named', including a struct. A value of type 'Named' must be an object of a class, and a struct value is not one. Change the return type of 'returned' to 'T', or bound 'T' by a class that implements 'Named', as in '<T: Person>'.
// @expect-error Element 1 has type 'T', but the elements of this array have type 'Named'. 'T' can be any type that implements 'Named', including a struct. A value of type 'Named' must be an object of a class, and a struct value is not one. Bound 'T' by a class that implements 'Named', as in '<T: Person>'.
// @expect-error This lambda must return 'Named', but its body has type 'T'. 'T' can be any type that implements 'Named', including a struct. A value of type 'Named' must be an object of a class, and a struct value is not one. Bound 'T' by a class that implements 'Named', as in '<T: Person>'.
// @expect-error The fallback after '??' has type 'T', but it replaces 'absent' when 'absent' is null, so it must have type 'Named'. 'T' can be any type that implements 'Named', including a struct. A value of type 'Named' must be an object of a class, and a struct value is not one. Bound 'T' by a class that implements 'Named', as in '<T: Person>'.
// @expect-error The fallback after '??' has type 'T', but it replaces 'absent' when 'absent' is null, so it must have type 'Named'. 'T' can be any type that implements 'Named', including a struct. A value of type 'Named' must be an object of a class, and a struct value is not one. Call the methods of 'Named' on 'value' directly, as in 'value.name()', or bound 'T' by a class that implements 'Named', as in '<T: Person>'.
// @expect-error The two results of this '?:' are 'T' and 'Named', which have no common type. 'T' can be any type that implements 'Named', including a struct. A value of type 'Named' must be an object of a class, and a struct value is not one. Bound 'T' by a class that implements 'Named', as in '<T: Person>'.
// @expect-error The two results of this '?:' are 'T' and 'Named', which have no common type. 'T' can be any type that implements 'Named', including a struct. A value of type 'Named' must be an object of a class, and a struct value is not one. Call the methods of 'Named' on 'value' directly, as in 'value.name()', or bound 'T' by a class that implements 'Named', as in '<T: Person>'.
// @expect-error Switch arms produce 'Named' and 'T', which have no common type. 'T' can be any type that implements 'Named', including a struct. A value of type 'Named' must be an object of a class, and a struct value is not one. Call the methods of 'Named' on 'value' directly, as in 'value.name()', or bound 'T' by a class that implements 'Named', as in '<T: Person>'.
// @expect-error Loop variable 'each' has type 'Named', but this loop gives it 'T' values. 'T' can be any type that implements 'Named', including a struct. A value of type 'Named' must be an object of a class, and a struct value is not one. Declare it as 'T each', or bound 'T' by a class that implements 'Named', as in '<T: Person>'.
